{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 RCA / design classification\n\nProven mechanism: `Makefile:203` runs `zizmor $(RELEASE_WORKFLOW)` with no explicit operating mode and no GitHub token. Zizmor 1.29 follows its documented selection rule: with GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN/ZIZMOR_GITHUB_TOKEN all absent it creates no GitHub client, defaults offline, warns, and skips exactly five token-backed audits: `impostor-commit`, `ref-confusion`, `known-vulnerable-actions`, `stale-action-refs`, and `ref-version-mismatch`. The remaining 35 audits run, the one intentional excessive-permissions suppression remains, and the process exits 0. Upstream source confirms each skipped audit’s `Audit::new` refuses a missing GitHub client; upstream Usage §Operating Modes defines this tokenless default.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: (A) bare tokenless zizmor scheduled 35, logged those five skips + the reported warning, and exited 0; (B) explicit `--offline` scheduled the same 35 and exited 0 without the warning; (C) a valid GH token scheduled all 40, made GitHub API requests, produced no warning, and exited 0. A deliberately invalid token scheduled all 40 but then failed the audit on a 401, proving online mode adds network/credential availability to the gate rather than only silencing output. A mismatched action version-comment mutation passed explicit offline but online reported seven `ref-version-mismatch` findings; offline mutations still caught the approved SHA-pin and excessive-permissions invariants.\n\nGerrit/CI proof: `_build-and-test.yml:16-19,40-46,90-91` says the reusable takes no secrets and invokes `make lint` without a token env. Actual successful Gerrit Verified run 32102186979 logged the same offline warning at 2026-08-18T05:17:25Z; successful mirror run 32086994835 did likewise. Thus both local and gating CI currently use identical offline semantics.\n\nLegitimacy classification: `intended-behavior` for the upstream warning/default and `feature-request` / design choice for making the five online audits mandatory. The authoritative story `footed-semiacidic-sable` requires zizmor under local `make lint`, scoped to release.yml, and explicitly names full-SHA pins, persist-credentials:false, and permissions; it never requires a token, network, warning-free output, or the full online audit set. The same warning/five skips occur with its introducing zizmor 1.27, so this is not a later regression. No repository authority resolves whether to expand that approved contract.\n\nRecommended non-fix disposition: keep `make lint` deterministic and explicit with `zizmor --offline` (documenting its existing 35-audit semantics and removing the warning). If the five live-metadata audits are desired, add a separate operation-linked online security target and invoke it from Gerrit/GitHub CI with least-privilege `GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}`; decide explicitly whether API outage/rate-limit is gate-fatal. Do not conditionally token the same `make lint`, because that would silently violate the pin’s stated local↔CI parity. No code change is authorized until the owner chooses the target contract.\n\nObserved residual: changing persist-credentials:false to true did not produce a default-persona zizmor finding in this workflow, although `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py::test_checkouts_disable_persist_credentials` independently enforces the invariant in the full CI suite. Accepted outside this online-mode decision because the invariant remains gated; the misleading “zizmor enforces” comment should be corrected with whichever policy change is approved."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787031774029471001,"uuid":"e5ba0836-3022-4cb1-9fd1-cbbb6e46b715"}